# SRG-APP-000246-WSR-000149  -  CAT II
# The web server must restrict the ability of users to launch Denial of
# Service (DoS) attacks against other information systems or networks.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000246-WSR-000149
group:           V-206409
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-001094
control_rev5:    SC-5

contribution:    Splunk Enterprise can limit the outbound traffic a user is able to make it
                 generate: the webhook alert action can be held to an allowlist of
                 endpoints rather than permitted to query any address, per-result alert
                 triggering is capped in both count and duration so one search cannot emit
                 unbounded notifications, and the capabilities that let a user run
                 arbitrary code or scripted actions are withheld from the built-in
                 non-administrative roles.

governs:         alert_actions.conf - What Splunk does when an alert fires, such as sending email or calling a
                 webhook.
governs:         authorize.conf - Used to create roles.
governs:         limits.conf - Limits on how much work searches and data processing may consume.

check:           alert_actions.conf [webhook] enable_allowlist equals true, plus a second condition requiring at least one key matching ^allowlist\. to be present in [webhook]
check:           limits.conf [scheduler] max_per_result_alerts not_equals 0
check:           limits.conf [scheduler] max_per_result_alerts_time not_equals 0
check:           authorize.conf [role_user] run_custom_command absent
check:           authorize.conf [role_user] edit_scripted absent
