external:        Egress filtering and rate limiting at the network boundary - firewall or
                 network component configuration
external:        The contents of the webhook endpoint allowlist (allowlist.<name>) -
                 organization-defined
external:        The alert result and concurrency caps appropriate to the platform's
                 capacity - organization-defined values informed by the deployment's sizing
external:        Review of locally defined roles beyond the built-in user role, which
                 configuration alone cannot classify as administrative or not -
                 organizational role design
external:        Outbound traffic generated by installed add-ons through their own code
                 rather than through alert actions - application review

citation:        alert_actions.conf.spec:605-615 ([webhook] enable_allowlist = <boolean>,
                 default false; "CAUTION ... Failure to do so is a security risk, as the
                 webhook alert action can then query against any endpoint, including
                 external endpoints that are not in your control and that could be
                 malicious"); alert_actions.conf.spec:617-620 (allowlist.<name> = <regular
                 expression>); limits.conf.spec:4056-4060 ([scheduler]
                 max_per_result_alerts, "Use 0 to disable this limit", default 500);
                 limits.conf.spec:4062-4066 (max_per_result_alerts_time, "Use 0 to disable
                 this limit", default 300); limits.conf.spec:4033-4035 (max_action_results,
                 default 50000); limits.conf.spec:4068-4072 (max_searches_perc, default
                 50); limits.conf.spec:457-463 ([search] max_searches_per_cpu, default 1);
                 authorize.conf.spec:67-72 ([role_<roleName>], "'enabled' is the only
                 accepted value here, as capabilities are disabled by default");
                 authorize.conf.spec:638 ([capability::edit_scripted]), :912
                 ([capability::run_custom_command]), :909 ([capability::run_dump]), :699
                 ([capability::edit_tcp]), :716 ([capability::edit_udp])
finding:         The application does not limit its use in a denial of service attack
                 against other systems to the extent the product allows: the webhook
                 endpoint allowlist is not enabled, a per-result alert cap is disabled by
                 being set to 0, or the built-in application user role has been granted a
                 capability that runs arbitrary code or scripted inputs.
